  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">People Centered Governance Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Somalia):  While Al-Shabaab serves as a credible alternative to the state in much of southern Somalia, it has not been able to transcend clan politics and struggles to provide inclusive or responsive governance. The 2022 uprisings in Hirshabelle are an example of al-Shabaab&apos;s failures to overcome these issues. Layering over prior stabilization efforts, USAID will strengthen legitimate and effective local governance as part of its efforts to offer an alternative to al-Shabaab rule in southern Somalia. Working in partnership with local, state, and federal governments, this program recognizes that efforts to consolidate prior stabilization gains will require a mixture of reconciliation and local governance programming. This program is designed to sequence and layer over other USAID/donor-funded inter-communal reconciliation and stabilization activities..With FY 2024 resources, USAID will support local governments to better manage resources and identify and respond to citizen priorities, improving the performance and quality of local governance in Somalia. Specifically, USAID will provide capacity building to established or emerging governance structures to deliver tangible improvements and promote participatory processes that seek citizen input to identify key needs and priorities. With FY 2024 resources, USAID will focus on providing a voice to youth, women, minorities, and marginalized groups to positively engage in, and contribute to, political processes. In particular, USAID will identify and support civil society and community-based organizations to represent and advocate citizen interests while holding the government to account. Recognizing that enabling communities to plan for future shocks and climate risks is key to effective governance, USAID will, whenever possible, work with local governance structures to strengthen their disaster risk-reduction efforts and contribute to Adaptation-Indirect....... .</narrative>
  </description>
